  "goodToKnow": "Die Fernwärme is district heating: hot water piped from a central plant, often a combined heat and power station (Kraft-Wärme-Kopplung), into homes. It's widespread in big cities and in eastern Germany's Plattenbau estates. The 2023 heating law (Heizungsgesetz) and municipal heat planning aim to expand it as part of the energy transition. It has no plural."
